From 900d511bf1d1921e11b5234de66151d74a5ded5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (review)" <review@localhost>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 09:14:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Stage 2: wall-clock deadlines, late completion discarded,
 bounded workers

- CallRunner: caller waits a wall-clock budget; a timed-out join does NOT
  cancel the request; late results are discarded (only caller threads write
  state). Bounded in-flight workers; saturation fails closed (reads
  UNAVAILABLE; submits NOT_SUBMITTED with nothing sent and no intent).
- read(): each attempt gets only the remaining budget; backoff never sleeps
  past it; slow-drip bounded by the caller deadline.
- submit: single POST on a reserved worker; DEADLINE -> UNRESOLVED, reconciled
  by the same client id.
- Integration fix: gateway tracks in-flight POSTs per client id; abandon and
  release refuse while the POST is in flight (found by combining stage 2 with
  round 3b; reproduced first).
- Workers inherit the caller thread name (tracing; preserved a round-2 fixture).

Tests: stage-2 suite 10 (7 fail on 127b6d0; 10 pass); stage-1 85 unchanged.
95/95; combined single-process runs and repeat runs stable.
